1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,456
Ridgeline Freight is a fictional logistics company with 24 internal documents.

2
00:00:06,756 --> 00:00:09,612
I'm logging in as a sales rep.

3
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:19,512
Every claim carries a citation.

4
00:00:19,812 --> 00:00:22,620
One click opens the clause.

5
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:29,184
The sources panel shows what was retrieved, with scores, cost and latency.

6
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:54,008
Comparison questions pull passages from two documents and attribute each figure to its source.

7
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:06,564
When the documents don't contain the answer, it says so.

8
00:01:06,864 --> 00:01:14,880
Refusals are enforced by the retrieval gate and by citation validation, not just by the prompt.

9
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,456
Access control lives in the SQL query.

10
00:01:21,756 --> 00:01:30,060
A sales user never retrieves a chunk from an HR document, and an automated test proves it for every role and question.

11
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:47,656
Quality is measured on a held-out test set: hit rate, correctness, faithfulness and refusal accuracy, with an independent judge model.

12
00:01:47,956 --> 00:01:51,004
Code and methodology are public.
